# The three 3,000.00 pairs are not interchangeable even though they look
# alike: each is paired with the half of its own date, closest date first.

$TBD
BusinessRule Which half pairs with which when several match
Description Closest date first, and then the order the files were read. A half
# that has been paired is out of the running for the rest.
Examples: CandidatePriority
| Test | Condition                                             |
| 1    | The pair whose dates are closest together is formed first |
| 2    | A tie goes to the earlier date                        |
| 3    | A further tie goes to the order the files were read   |
| 4    | A half already paired is not offered again            |

Attributes CandidatePriority
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Test      | Integer | 0       |
| Condition | String  |         |

Scenario A candidate is never proposed within one account
Description Two transactions in one account with opposite amounts is a payment
# and a refund, or a mistake, and either way it is not a transfer.
# The rule in Transactions refuses a transaction transaction twice to one
# account, and this is where that is kept from arising.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type     | Placeholder | BankId    | AccountNumber |
| Assets:Checking Prime  | Checking | false       | 053000219 | 1023711843105 |
| Assets:Checking        | Checking | false       | 053000219 | 1023711843112 |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense  | false       | none      | none          |
| Income:Uncategorized   | Income   | false       | none      | none          |
When statements imported : OfxImportFile
| OfxAccountId  | TrnType | DatePosted | Amount  | FitId | Name     |
| 1023711843105 | DEBIT   | 2026-08-03 | -120.00 | S1    | A SHOP   |
| 1023711843105 | CREDIT  | 2026-08-04 | 120.00  | S2    | A REFUND |
Then transfer candidates are : TransferCandidate
| FromAccount | FromDate | ToAccount | ToDate | Amount | DaysApart | State |
# No rows.

# Left $TBD: the card half's OfxAccountId below (4111111111111333) is the
# number of no account in the chart this scenario declares, so as written it
# cannot be attributed to any account at all -- yet the Then step expects
# New=1, which only the card half could supply. Either Liabilities:WF Card,
# carrying that number, is missing from this scenario, or a number no account
# claims is meant in a multi-file import to do something other than
# contribute nothing, and either way that is a decision for the spec's
# author, not a glue fix.
$TBD
Scenario A candidate is not proposed when one half matches a transaction already there
Description The matching rules of this file run first. A downloaded transaction
# that clears something already in the book is accounted for, and is
# not then also offered as half of a transfer.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
